# gemini-decision-1 environment file template. Copy it to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in
# only the lines you need. Every line below is commented out, so this file sets nothing.
#
#   bash:        cp .env.example .env.local
#   PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
#
# Lookup: .env.local, then .env, in the package folder (the gemini-decision-1 folder itself, not
# the folder you are working in), then in GEMINI_CORE_HOME. A variable that is already set and not
# empty in the shell always wins. The first file that sets a variable wins. Only GEMINI_* and
# GOOGLE_API_KEY are read. Never commit a file that holds a real key.
#
# Put comments on their own lines: a value is everything after the "=" on that line.

# Gemini calls are billed to this key. Heuristic mode needs no key at all.
# GEMINI_API_KEY takes precedence over GOOGLE_API_KEY when both are set.
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Mode: auto (default; Gemini, falling back to the rules), gemini (strict; a Gemini failure fails the
# decision), or heuristic (rules only; no network, no key).
# GEMINI_CORE_MODE=auto

# Decisions API endpoint and model. Changing the URL sends the decision texts and the key there.
# GEMINI_DECISION_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/decisions
# GEMINI_DECISION_MODEL=gemini-decision-1

# Per-call timeout in milliseconds (a positive integer). A timeout pauses Gemini for 30 seconds.
# GEMINI_DECISION_TIMEOUT_MS=4000

# Below this confidence Gemini abstains and the rules decide. A number from 0 to 1.
# GEMINI_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.4

# Home folder for memory.jsonl, decisions.jsonl and config.json. Default: ~/.gemini-decision-1.
# Set it in the shell, not in an env file, so that the env files are found in the same place.
# GEMINI_CORE_HOME=

# Path to a JSON config file. Relative paths resolve from the current folder.
# GEMINI_CORE_CONFIG=
